# Security headers applied to every route (Netlify).
# CSP allows self + Google Fonts (CSS from googleapis, font files from gstatic),
# inline styles (React style props / prerendered inline CSS) and inline scripts
# (the JSON-LD structured-data blocks in the page head + Netlify's injected RUM
# script + the gtag.js bootstrap). Google Analytics (GA4): gtag.js is loaded
# from googletagmanager.com (script-src), and measurement hits go to
# google-analytics.com (connect-src for the fetch beacon, img-src for the pixel
# fallback). connect-src also allows Netlify's Real User Metrics beacon
# (ingesteer.services-prod.nsvcs.net) so RUM isn't blocked. Microsoft Clarity:
# the inline bootstrap snippet loads www.clarity.ms/tag/<id>, which in turn
# loads the real engine from scripts.clarity.ms/<version>/clarity.js — so
# script-src must allow *.clarity.ms (www alone is NOT enough; with only www
# the bootstrap loads but the engine is silently blocked and the dashboard
# shows 0 sessions/heatmaps even though the tag is present). Session uploads
# go to b.clarity.ms (connect-src *.clarity.ms) and a sync pixel is fetched
# from c.clarity.ms/c.gif (img-src *.clarity.ms).
# frame-src allows instagram.com so blog posts can embed a Reel via its
# /embed iframe. There is deliberately no script-src entry for Instagram: we
# use the plain iframe, not their embed.js, so none of their JavaScript runs
# on our origin. Without frame-src the iframe is blocked, because frame-src
# otherwise falls back to default-src 'self'. Google Tag Manager: the GTM
# container script itself loads from googletagmanager.com (already allowed
# for GA4's gtag.js), and its <noscript> fallback embeds an iframe from the
# same host, so frame-src needs an explicit entry too. Meta Pixel: the
# bootstrap snippet loads fbevents.js from connect.facebook.net (script-src),
# and every tracked event (including the <noscript> fallback pixel) is a
# beacon/image hit to www.facebook.com/tr — allowed in both connect-src (the
# JS beacon) and img-src (the noscript <img> fallback when JS is disabled).
# Google Ads (gtag.js config 'AW-...', see the GA4 script above): conversion
# linking pings and the sync pixel go to www.google.com and
# www.googleadservices.com — allowed in both connect-src (the fetch/beacon
# hit) and img-src (the pixel fallback), same pattern as the GA4 entries.
# Google Ads view-through conversions + Floodlight/GTM conversion linking
# (flagged blocked by Google Tag Assistant): view-through conversion pixels
# are requested from googleads.g.doubleclick.net/pagead/viewthroughconversion/...
# and cross-domain conversion-linking "collect" hits go to
# ad.doubleclick.net/ccm/s/collect. Both can fire as either a fetch/beacon
# or a plain <img> depending on browser support, so both domains are
# allowed in connect-src and img-src (same dual-directive pattern as the
# other Google/Meta entries above). No script-src entry is needed — neither
# URL loads a script, both are data-collection endpoints only.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.clarity.ms https://*.clarity.ms https://connect.facebook.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://www.clarity.ms https://*.clarity.ms https://www.facebook.com https://www.google.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://ad.doubleclick.net; connect-src 'self' https://ingesteer.services-prod.nsvcs.net https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.clarity.ms https://*.clarity.ms https://www.facebook.com https://connect.facebook.net https://www.google.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://ad.doubleclick.net; frame-src https://www.instagram.com https://instagram.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
